Your chance for getting artifact gifts and also for
successfully wishing for artifacts goes down as more
artifacts enter the game. I don't think the invocation items
count in either case. The odds of gaining an artifact by
wishing begin going down once there are two artifacts
created. If I were wishing, I would wish for Grayswindr, the
blasting won't be that bad.

I don't think it's unusual to see 5 or 6 artifacts during a
game. I know I've been given three or four in some recent
games. If you are praying during your sac fest you could go
on forever without getting a weapon. The best weapons for a
neutral character are Frost Brand, Fire Brand, Mojo and
Magicbane. I'd take any of those before Vorpral Blade
anyway. To make Magicbane viable you need to two weapon with
a silver saber, long sword, katana or trident. A crysknife
is almost as good if you just like them, but you should be
two weaponing in any case.

Other than the 5% beheading, VB is only 1/2 point damage
better than an ordinary long sword and does less damage than
a katana or trident. You could wield two of those non
artifact weapons and succeed, I suspect. The bonus for VB
"to hit" doesn't much help an advanced character with max
luck.

You could convert to lawful and dip a long sword for
Excalibur. I have ascended a samurai with Excalibur and a
katana.
